NYC Payroll Data Integration using Azure
Project Overview

This project builds an end-to-end data integration and analytics pipeline for the City of New York payroll data using Azure services.
The goal is to analyze how payroll and overtime costs are distributed across city agencies and make the aggregated data available for analytics using Azure Synapse Analytics.

The solution uses Azure Data Factory to ingest, transform, and aggregate payroll data from Azure Data Lake Gen2 into Azure SQL Database, and finally exposes summarized data through Synapse external tables.

Architecture Overview

Data Flow:

Azure Data Lake Gen2 (CSV files)
→ Azure Data Factory (Data Flows & Pipelines)
→ Azure SQL Database (Staging & Summary tables)
→ Azure Data Lake Gen2 (dirstaging)
→ Azure Synapse Analytics (External Table)

Azure Services Used

Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 – Source and staging storage

Azure Data Factory (ADF) – Data ingestion, transformation, orchestration

Azure SQL Database – Master, transaction, and summary tables

Azure Synapse Analytics (Serverless SQL Pool) – Analytics using external tables

GitHub – Version control for ADF artifacts

Source Data

The source data consists of CSV files stored in Azure Data Lake Gen2:

Master Data

EmpMaster.csv

AgencyMaster.csv

TitleMaster.csv

Payroll Data

nycpayroll_2020.csv

nycpayroll_2021.csv

Data Model
SQL Tables Created

NYC_Payroll_EMP_MD

NYC_Payroll_AGENCY_MD

NYC_Payroll_TITLE_MD

NYC_Payroll_Data_2020

NYC_Payroll_Data_2021

NYC_Payroll_Summary

Data Flows
Master Data Flows

Load Employee, Agency, and Title master data from Data Lake to SQL Database

Payroll Data Flows

Load 2020 and 2021 payroll data from Data Lake to SQL Database

Aggregation Data Flow

Union payroll data from 2020 and 2021

Calculate TotalPaid = RegularGrossPaid + TotalOTPaid + TotalOtherPay

Aggregate by AgencyName and FiscalYear

Write results to:

SQL summary table

Data Lake dirstaging folder

Pipeline Orchestration

The Azure Data Factory pipeline executes data flows in the following order:

Master data flows (run in parallel)

Payroll data flows (run after master data)

Aggregation data flow (runs last)

All pipeline activities are implemented using Execute Data Flow activities.

Data Validation

Verified summary data in Azure SQL Database

Verified files created in Data Lake Gen2 (dirstaging)

Queried aggregated results using Synapse external table
